node_modules
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
dist
# Build OUTPUT folders, not sources. They hold image tarballs and the site's own
# .env, so leaving them in the context copies real secrets into the intermediate
# build layer and adds a slow multi-GB transfer to every build.
#
# Matched by prefix rather than named one at a time: dist-onprem/ and
# dist-new-customer/ were missed by the old explicit list and together carried
# 3.1 GB and two live client .env files into the context. A top-level `.env`
# rule does not save you here — .dockerignore matches whole paths, so `.env`
# never matches `dist-onprem/.env`.
dist-*/
coverage
*.log
.idea
.vscode
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile*
README.md
test
